Every record carries `raster` + top-level `gate_snn` + `gate_compute` + `snn_tags`. Windows {wins[0]:.0f}/{wins[1]:.0f}/{wins[2]:.0f} ms; `window_s == window_ms/1000` exactly; `spikes == round(neurons·rate·window_s)` with zero slack ({n_sp[0]}/{n_sp[1]}/{n_sp[2]} at {rates[0]}/{rates[1]}/{rates[2]} Hz over {n_neu[0]}/{n_neu[1]}/{n_neu[2]} neurons); `energy_pJ = spikes·23` and `energy_uJ = spikes·23e-6` exact ({n_sp[0]*23}/{n_sp[1]*23}/{n_sp[2]*23} pJ). Routing source/target + 3-entry tables + `third_factor` on all three (modulators {tfs[0]} / {tfs[1]} / {tfs[2]}; τe {taus[0]}/{taus[1]}/{taus[2]} s as consistent `tau_e_s`+`tau_e_ms` pairs). Excerpts are **independent CUBA LIF** first-passage times (not a re-encode of `spike_events`; Jaccard {jacs[0]:.4f}/{jacs[1]:.4f}/{jacs[2]:.4f}), integer `t_us`, in-window, `neuron_id`-bounded, sorted, full-window by construction, per-spike amplitude with adaptation (0.82**k) plus noise; excerpt span ≥ 1000 µs ({spans[0]}/{spans[1]}/{spans[2]} µs). ISI histograms from the FULL window, bins ≥1 ms, counts sum to `spikes − distinct_active_neurons` ({isis[0]}/{isis[1]}/{isis[2]}). Same-neuron gaps ≥1000 µs serialized. `gate_snn` on all three: decisions REJECT/MODIFY/ACCEPT matching each lead trajectory **and** matching `snn_tags`; every rate-declaring population's budget exact against its decision window. `gate_compute.per_check` windows 32–40 ms, budgets exact ({gc[0]} / {gc[1]} / {gc[2]}). Required `meta.snn_tags`, `meta.nelb.snn_tags`, top-level `snn_tags`, and `gate_snn.snn_tags` = [race, refractory, adaptation] on every record. Main streams: {events[0]}/{events[1]}/{events[2]} events (48+; leftover-mill r23 was 32/31/30), strictly increasing `t_rel_ms` only (no `t_ms` mix), same-channel refractory ≥0.8 ms (a1 GD-OES pair at 1.4 ms, a2 NV pair at 1.2 ms, a3 self-mixing pair at 1.5 ms). Independent LIF seeds 2026092301/2026092302/2026092303 (no shared LIF state).

## Self-critique

### Edge cases added vs still thin
- **Added:** first GD-OES remaining-Sn-coating family on a tinplate line with a recomputable sputter-voltage table (`15.00 µm` vs lumped-k `12.00`); first NV-center ODMR remaining-current family on a chlorate HIL dummy with a recomputable T0/T table (`40.00 kA` vs lumped-k `32.00`) plus bus-power identity and timezone-skipped microwave-AE exoneration; first self-mixing remaining-vibration family on a mill gearbox with a recomputable λ/λ0 table (`20.00 µm` vs lumped-k `16.00`) plus velocity identity and bounded ACCEPT of G-6 only; 52-event streams vs leftover-mill r23 32/31/30; independent CUBA LIF plus required matching snn_tags (leftover-mill r23 lacked snn_tags); operational t2 on all three; provenance trio designed/hil/simulated; 18/24/12 min slow floors in-stream.
- **Still thin:** (i) a1's V0 column is constant — a voltage-zero hop that fakes 15.00 µm inside a 1.80 Plateveil corridor is unwritten; (ii) a2 still has a plant-owned bus voltage; a booth whose millivolt rides the colluding Odveil bus, so the gate must refuse with *only* microwave-lock AE plus pass log, is harder (vendor-only lead REJECT remains open, as r22 flagged); (iii) a3's k_s is a lumped µm/fringe at λ0, not a speckle / working-distance map, so a 20 mm standoff hop that fakes 20.00 µm is unwritten; (iv) stream amplitudes remain authored constants (raster draws are the only seeded LIF noise); (v) no gate_snn input→output volley pair at raster resolution this round.

### Realism of noise / temporal fidelity
- Strong: a1's 15.00 µm, lumped 12.00, mass 12.00, V/V0 1.25, and 18.0 min hold (`6000+1080=7080 s`) recompute from the record; a2's 40.00 kA, lumped 32.00, P 160.00, T0/T 1.25, and 24.0 min new-head (`2820+1440=4260 s`) recompute; a3's 20.00 µm, lumped 16.00, v 5.00, λ/λ0 1.25, and 12.0 min survey (`6000+720=6720 s`) recompute. Independent CUBA LIF (tau_m 10/12/8 ms) plus 0.82**k adaptation and 1.2–1.5 ms physics pairs give the 52-event stream a raster-scale motif without violating 0.8 ms same-channel refractory or 1000 µs same-neuron excerpt gaps.
- **Gaps, honestly:** (i) 52 events still thins 1 Hz GD-OES / kHz NV lock-in / kHz self-mixing stacks; (ii) a1's post-stop 20.00 µm is a later sample, not a closed-loop line-hold controller; (iii) a2 HIL coupon times an in-service isolate that the stream does not independently witness on a second live bus until the new head starts; (iv) leftover-mill r23 LIT anisotropy / TFM skip-path / EN PSD leftovers were not restaged here (new families instead).

### Training value (SNN/LSM + agentic)
Distillation targets: GD-OES t=k_g·(I_sn/I_fe)·(V/V0) plus voltage-table SoT vs lumped-k fail; conjunctive isolate floor vs continue-coat vs hall ESD; Plateveil-infra collusion; NV I=k_n·Δf·(T0/T) plus T-table SoT and bus-power identity; isolate-floor bus vs keep-whole vs hall dump; microwave-lock AE / timezone exoneration; self-mixing d=k_s·N·(λ/λ0) and velocity identities; bounded ACCEPT with G-1/G-2/G-5-out-of-scope; skip-survey refusal under survey takt. Agentic value concentrates in three patterns: reconstruction-as-SoT on a physical coating/current/vibration the raw corridor cannot see (with a table that makes lumped-k fail), earned ACCEPT with an explicit physical out-of-scope object (G-1/G-2/G-5), and stop-then-hold so a REJECT does not become a hall/hall/mill kill. Independent LIF rasters give Spikenaut a non-echo membrane crossing to distill against the language view.

## What round 24 should add (next densification target)
1. **V0-drift row** on a non-ST-4 GD-OES so a zero hop fakes 15.00 µm inside a 1.80 Plateveil corridor, closing a1's constant-V0 leftover.
